deleting data first, then auth. If auth fails, prompt them to re-login. Since   
data is already deleted, if they re-login and try again, deleteAllUserData will 
just do nothing (or delete 0 docs), and then user.delete() should work because  
they just logged in. This is a reasonable flow.                                 

